                            span a 224 14902 28 16 link 477
                            text "In July 2012, WHATWG and " 48 14902 176 16 serif 16
                            text "W3C" 224 14902 28 16 serif 16 underline link 477
                            text " decided on a degree" 252 14902 136 16 serif 16
                          line 48 14920 344 20 base 14
                            text "of separation. W3C will continue the HTML5" 48 14922 280 16 serif 16
                          line 48 14940 344 20 base 14
                            text "specification work, focusing on a single definitive" 48 14942 324 16 serif 16
                          line 48 14960 344 20 base 14
                            text "standard, which is considered a \"snapshot\" by" 48 14962 308 16 serif 16
                          line 48 14980 344 20 base 14
                            text "WHATWG. The WHATWG organization will continue its" 48 14982 340 16 serif 16
                          line 48 15000 344 20 base 14
                            text "work with HTML5 as a \"Living Standard\". The" 48 15002 296 16 serif 16
                          line 48 15020 344 20 base 14
                            text "concept of a living standard is that it is never" 48 15022 292 16 serif 16
                          line 48 15040 344 20 base 14
                            text "complete and is always being updated and" 48 15042 280 16 serif 16
                          line 48 15060 344 20 base 14
                            text "improved. New features can be added but" 48 15062 268 16 serif 16
