                      block p 8 31504 384 60
                        line 8 31504 384 20 base 14
                          text "The Frameset version includes everything in the" 8 31506 312 16 serif 16
                        line 8 31524 384 20 base 14
                          span code 240 31526 64 16
                          text "Transitional version, as well as the " 8 31526 232 16 serif 16
                          text "frameset" 240 31526 64 16 mono 16
                          text " element" 304 31526 56 16 serif 16
                        line 8 31544 384 20 base 14
                          span code 120 31546 32 16
                          span code 216 31546 40 16
                          text "(used instead of " 8 31546 112 16 serif 16
                          text "body" 120 31546 32 16 mono 16
                          text ") and the " 152 31546 64 16 serif 16
                          text "frame" 216 31546 40 16 mono 16
                          text " element." 256 31546 60 16 serif 16
                    block section 8 31583 384 142
                      block div 8 31583 384 23
                        block h3 8 31583 384 23
                          line 8 31583 384 23 base 16
                            text "Frameset versus transitional" 8 31585 219 19 serif 19 bold
                      block p 8 31625 384 100
                        line 8 31625 384 20 base 14
                          text "In addition to the above transitional differences, the" 8 31627 336 16 serif 16
                        line 8 31645 384 20 base 14
                          text "frameset specifications (whether XHTML 1.0 or HTML 4.01)" 8 31647 376 16 serif 16
                        line 8 31665 384 20 base 14
                          span code 260 31667 64 16
                          text "specify a different content model, with " 8 31667 252 16 serif 16
                          text "frameset" 260 31667 64 16 mono 16
                          text " replacing" 324 31667 64 16 serif 16
                        line 8 31685 384 20 base 14
                          span code 8 31687 32 16
                          span code 176 31687 40 16
                          text "body" 8 31687 32 16 mono 16
                          text ", that contains either " 40 31687 136 16 serif 16
                          text "frame" 176 31687 40 16 mono 16
                          text " elements, or optionally" 216 31687 152 16 serif 16
                        line 8 31705 384 20 base 14
                          span code 8 31707 64 16
                          span code 120 31707 32 16
                          text "noframes" 8 31707 64 16 mono 16
                          text " with a " 72 31707 48 16 serif 16
                          text "body" 120 31707 32 16 mono 16
                          text "." 152 31707 4 16 serif 16
                    block section 8 31744 384 638
                      block div 8 31744 384 24
                        block h3 8 31744 384 24
                          line 8 31744 384 24 base 16
                            text "Summary of specification versions" 8 31746 266 19 serif 19 bold
                      block p 8 31786 384 400
                        line 8 31786 384 20 base 14
                          text "As this list demonstrates, the loose versions of the" 8 31788 328 16 serif 16
                        line 8 31806 384 20 base 14
                          text "specification are maintained for legacy support. However," 8 31808 372 16 serif 16
                        line 8 31826 384 20 base 14
                          text "contrary to popular misconceptions, the move to XHTML" 8 31828 360 16 serif 16
                        line 8 31846 384 20 base 14
                          text "does not imply a removal of this legacy support. Rather the" 8 31848 380 16 serif 16
                        line 8 31866 384 20 base 14
                          text "X in XML stands for extensible and the W3C is modularizing" 8 31868 384 16 serif 16
                        line 8 31886 384 20 base 14
                          text "the entire specification and opens it up to independent" 8 31888 352 16 serif 16
                        line 8 31906 384 20 base 14
                          text "extensions. The primary achievement in the move from" 8 31908 356 16 serif 16
                        line 8 31926 384 20 base 14
                          text "XHTML 1.0 to XHTML 1.1 is the modularization of the entire" 8 31928 364 16 serif 16
                        line 8 31946 384 20 base 14
                          text "specification. The strict version of HTML is deployed in" 8 31948 356 16 serif 16
                        line 8 31966 384 20 base 14
                          text "XHTML 1.1 through a set of modular extensions to the base" 8 31968 372 16 serif 16
                        line 8 31986 384 20 base 14
                          text "XHTML 1.1 specification. Likewise, someone looking for the" 8 31988 380 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32006 384 20 base 14
                          text "loose (transitional) or frameset specifications will find" 8 32008 356 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32026 384 20 base 14
                          text "similar extended XHTML 1.1 support (much of it is contained" 8 32028 384 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32046 384 20 base 14
                          text "in the legacy or frame modules). Modularization also" 8 32048 344 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32066 384 20 base 14
                          text "allows for separate features to develop on their own" 8 32068 336 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32086 384 20 base 14
                          text "timetable. So for example, XHTML 1.1 will allow quicker" 8 32088 352 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32106 384 20 base 14
                          span a 308 32108 52 16 link 647
                          text "migration to emerging XML standards such as " 8 32108 300 16 serif 16
                          text "MathML" 308 32108 52 16 serif 16 underline link 647
                          text " (a" 360 32108 20 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32126 384 20 base 14
                          text "presentational and semantic math language based on" 8 32128 348 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32146 384 20 base 14
                          span a 76 32148 48 16 link 648
                          text "XML) and " 8 32148 68 16 serif 16
                          text "XForms" 76 32148 48 16 serif 16 underline link 648
                          text "—a new highly advanced web-form" 124 32148 228 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32166 384 20 base 14
                          text "technology to replace the existing HTML forms." 8 32168 304 16 serif 16
                      block p 8 32202 384 180
                        line 8 32202 384 20 base 14
                          text "In summary, the HTML 4 specification primarily reined in" 8 32204 368 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32222 384 20 base 14
                          text "all the various HTML implementations into a single clearly" 8 32224 376 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32242 384 20 base 14
                          text "written specification based on SGML. XHTML 1.0, ported this" 8 32244 384 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32262 384 20 base 14
                          text "specification, as is, to the new XML-defined specification." 8 32264 380 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32282 384 20 base 14
                          text "Next, XHTML 1.1 takes advantage of the extensible nature of" 8 32284 380 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32302 384 20 base 14
                          text "XML and modularizes the whole specification. XHTML 2.0" 8 32304 372 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32322 384 20 base 14
                          text "was intended to be the first step in adding new features to" 8 32324 376 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32342 384 20 base 14
                          text "the specification in a standards-body-based" 8 32344 292 16 serif 16
                        line 8 32362 384 20 base 14
                          span span 72 32367 7 13
                          span span 79 32367 78 13
                          span span 79 32367 78 13
                          span a 79 32367 78 13 link 649
                          span i 79 32367 78 13
                          span span 157 32367 6 13
                          span sup 72 32367 91 13
                          text "approach." 8 32364 64 16 serif 16
                          text "[" 72 32367 7 13 serif 13
                          text "AI-generated?" 79 32367 78 13 serif 13 italic underline link 649
                          text "]" 157 32367 6 13 serif 13
